{
  "name": "Kiron Labs - BarMon - Telegram Approval v1",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "sticky-overview",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -600,
        -380
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 760,
        "height": 340,
        "content": "## BarMon — Telegram Approval v1 (v2)\n\nOwn Telegram Trigger bound to BarMon's own bot (per the hybrid architecture: the Engine holds no client identity, so each client's Caller AND Approval workflow use their own bot credential). Listens for the Approve/Discard button taps sent by the Facebook/Instagram Caller's \"Send Draft for Review\" node, matches the row in `BarMon-Content` by a HASH PREFIX (not exact match — see note below), and updates its status.\n\n**Hash matching fix:** `callback_data` carries only the first 16 chars of `content_hash` (Telegram's `callback_data` has a 64-byte limit — a full SHA-256 plus the prefix would overflow it). This workflow matches with `startsWith`, same convention as the production Rob-LinkedIn workflow.\n\n**Who approves:** confirm with Rob before activating — kickoff assumption is Rob approves initially (the cousin/valuador isn't in the content loop yet).\n\n**Publish stays manual:** approving here does NOT post to Facebook/Instagram. It just marks the row `approved` so Rob knows it's cleared to post by hand.\n\n**Credentials needed:**\n- `Telegram - BarMon` (must be the SAME bot used by the Callers' \"Send Draft for Review\" node, so this Trigger receives that bot's callback_query updates)\n- `Google Sheets - Rob` (reused — same automation Google account as the Engine/Callers)\n- `Telegram - Rob` (ops channel, Error Trigger branch only)\n\n**Setup note:** after importing, set this bot's webhook/polling in n8n (Telegram Trigger handles this automatically once the credential is attached and the workflow is activated)."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "telegram-trigger",
      "name": "Telegram Trigger - BarMon Bot",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegramTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        -600,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "updates": [
          "callback_query"
        ]
      },
      "credentials": {
        "telegramApi": {
          "id": "",
          "name": "Telegram - BarMon"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "code-parse-callback",
      "name": "Parse Callback",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -360,
        0
      ],
      "notes": "Extracts action + short_hash from callback_data (format: 'barmon_approve|<16-char hash>' or 'barmon_discard|<16-char hash>' — pipe separator and truncated hash, matching what the Callers actually send). Flags anything else as invalid instead of throwing, since a shared bot could in theory receive unrelated callbacks.",
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const cb = $json.callback_query;\nconst data = cb && cb.data ? cb.data : '';\nconst [prefix, shortHash] = data.split('|');\nconst actionMap = { barmon_approve: 'approved', barmon_discard: 'discarded' };\nconst valid = Boolean(shortHash) && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(actionMap, prefix);\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    valid,\n    action: valid ? actionMap[prefix] : null,\n    short_hash: shortHash || null,\n    callback_query_id: cb ? cb.id : null,\n    chat_id: cb && cb.message ? cb.message.chat.id : null,\n    message_id: cb && cb.message ? cb.message.message_id : null,\n    original_text: cb && cb.message ? cb.message.text : '',\n    approver_name: cb && cb.from ? (cb.from.first_name || cb.from.username || 'desconocido') : 'desconocido'\n  }\n}];"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "if-valid-callback",
      "name": "Valid BarMon Callback?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        -120,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.valid }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "noop-ignore",
      "name": "Ignore - Not BarMon Callback",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        120,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "sheets-read-content",
      "name": "Read BarMon-Content",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        120,
        -80
      ],
      "notes": "Reads the full tab and matches by hash prefix in the next Code node — same pattern as the Engine, kept consistent on purpose. documentId is BarMon's real spreadsheet (19VRjs_zOnaTmHaFqSDIXKMnU5gVccBD7zP0Wx4Z8de0), same file used by the Callers.",
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "read",
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "19VRjs_zOnaTmHaFqSDIXKMnU5gVccBD7zP0Wx4Z8de0"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "BarMon-Content"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "credentials": {
        "googleSheetsOAuth2Api": {
          "id": "IcCapGhz6b79YwIJ",
          "name": "Google Sheets - Rob"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "code-find-row",
      "name": "Find Row by Hash",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        360,
        -80
      ],
      "notes": "Matches by startsWith, not equality — callback_data only carries the first 16 chars of the full content_hash stored in Sheets.",
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const ctx = $('Parse Callback').first().json;\nconst row = items.find(i => (i.json.content_hash || '').startsWith(ctx.short_hash));\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    ...ctx,\n    content_hash: row ? row.content_hash : null,\n    row_found: Boolean(row),\n    current_status: row ? row.status : null,\n    draft_content: row ? row.draft_content : null\n  }\n}];"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "if-row-found",
      "name": "Row Found?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
